# Canopy Vista: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls a Forest (one
# basic) and a Savannah (the Forest and Plains types, but not basic, CR 205.4c): one basic is below the two, so its Canopy
# Vista enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with a Forest and a Plains of
# its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Savannah
Canopy Vista
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Plains
Canopy Vista
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Savannah.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Canopy Vista.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Canopy Vista.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Canopy Vista.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Canopy Vista.Tapped = false
